# Naming and Single-Responsibility Audit: Reconciled Consensus, Dispositions
File: openOODA/audits/naming/consensus_dispositions.oot

Provenance: converted from `openOODA/audits/naming-audit-consensus.md` (256 lines). Part 2 of 2.

Redaction note: fleet host names and tailnet addresses are written as generic
placeholders. The audited tree still holds the literals.

## 4. Divergences — adjudicated

Table columns: # | Dispute | Devin | mcode | Evidence | **Consensus ruling**
- 4.1 | DE shell-host naming | Keep `oofiles`/`oopanel` names | RENAME → `ooshell`/`oogrant`; §6.1 wrongly lists `ooshell` as
  RFC ghost | `ooshell` appears in **no** governing doc — verified fleet-wide | **Keep `oopanel`/`oofiles`/`ooportal` names.**
  `ooshell` is mcode's invented proposal (marked [ERRATA] as an "RFC ghost"); `ooportal` matches the freedesktop pattern,
  `ooshell` would collide conceptually with tools `oosh`. Scope fix, not rename.
- 4.2 | `oomail`/`oochat` | Prefer `oomail` host (RFC; superset domain) | Lists `oomail`→`oochat` archive uncontested | RFC
  `:143` L5: `oomail` canonical, `oochat` absent; `oochat/personas/oomail/` (4 impl pages) > standalone `oomail` | **DECISION
  REQUIRED.** Two coherent rulings: (a) RFC-faithful — `oomail` canonical comms host, `oochat`→persona; (b) pragmatic — keep
  `oochat` host (larger impl, already embedded) + amend RFC to swap. Either way the loser is archived and the winner keeps the
  bigger impl. Neither audit may pick unilaterally.
- 4.3 | `ooarchitect` host | flagged dup, no pick | arbitration needed; noted divergent impls | `oogovern/ooarchitect/`
  byte-identical to standalone; `oooda-engine`'s variant drops `ooarch_basename` | **`oogovern`** — byte-identical copy
  preserves single-source-of-truth; retire `oooda-engine`'s divergent variant.
- 4.4 | `oohealthd`/`ooinit` | fold OR keep canonical | SPLIT `healthd/` out of `ooinit` | **RFC `:140` L2 list explicitly
  includes `oohealthd`**; `ooinit/healthd/`=8 pages; standalone repo ships `bin/oohealthd` | **`oohealthd` stays canonical per
  RFC — strip `ooinit/healthd/` embed.** (A prior consensus draft claimed "RFC L2 has no oohealthd" — [ERRATA], the name is
  literally in the list.) mcode's split verdict lands at the same endpoint: one owner, the canonical repo. Keep `oosvc-mgr`
  inside `ooinit`.
- 4.5 | `oocode`/`ooreviewer` | un-invert per RFC (`oocode` canonical) | demote `oocode` into `ooreviewer` — but §5.6 KEEP
  table lists **both**, internally inconsistent | RFC `:145` L7 has `oocode`, no `ooreviewer`; `ooreviewer/oocode/` = 30 pages
  | **`oocode` canonical; `ooreviewer` demoted to persona** (review is a coding-agent mode). Strip the inverted
  `ooreviewer/oocode/` subtree. If owner wants both as products, RFC needs a 9th slot — owner decision.
- 4.6 | `-cloud` suffix | noted collision | RENAME `oodns-cloud`/`oosched-cloud`/`ooregistry-cloud` → drop suffix |
  `tools/oodns` exists → `oodns-cloud`→`oodns` would *create* a stem collision | **Do not rename.** The suffix is load-bearing
  disambiguation on the install PATH. Resolution = absorption into `oomesh`/`oodeploy`/`oostore`, which makes the repo names
  moot anyway.
- 4.7 | `oob3sum` vs `oohash` | digest overlap noted, no owner pick | spec ambiguous — RFC→`oob3sum`, directive→`oohash` |
  mutual persona cycle verified; directive lists `oohash`, RFC §2.2.4 lists `oob3sum` | **Recommend `oohash` as the single
  digest host** — on naming grounds (this audit's own criterion): the host serves sha256/sha512/md5/cksum/b3sum personas; naming
  a multi-algorithm host after one algorithm (`oob3sum`) is the same overclaim defect flagged elsewhere. Break the mutual cycle,
  archive `oob3sum`→persona, **amend RFC** (or keep `oob3sum` + amend directive — owner picks; one owner mandatory). `oosha256`/
  `oosha512`/`oomd5`/`oocksum`→personas.
- 4.8 | `core` names clean? | "cleanest org; names honest" | `lsp`/`mcp`/`cli`/`tui`/`opm` = generic global names +
  artifact-name mismatch | `mcp/Makefile:26`→`dist/mcp` vs CI `ooda-mcp`; `install.sh:105` bare names | **Names are honest (D)
  but non-namespaced (M).** Ship artifacts uniformly as `ooda-lsp`/`ooda-mcp` (already CI names); retire bare `lsp`/`mcp`/`cli`/
  `tui`/`opm` from `~/.openooda/bin`. Repo renames `oocli`/`ootui`/`oopm` = optional, lower priority.
- 4.9 | `oosession`→`ooauthd` | proposed rename | ghost noted, no rename target | `oosession/policy/`=8 pages; RFC keeps
  `ooauthd` | **Rename `oosession`→`ooauthd`** (session+policy IS the auth daemon) — closes the ghost + names the domain
  correctly.
- 4.10 | Nested personas (host is itself a persona) | `oocockpit` nesting noted | `oocockpit`,`oolock` "host is also a persona"
  → demote | dispatch tables verified | **Flatten: a canonical host must not itself be a persona of another host.** `oocockpit`,
  `oolock`,`ooreviewer`→persona-only; `ooagent-hud` subtree → `oopanel` (or re-canonicalized per RFC).
- 4.11 | `oobazaar` | 4 backends = overlap | SPLIT per backend | `oobazaar/README.md:5-9` verified 4 install backends | **Keep
  one store; thin backend adapters** (bazaar=store is an honest name; 4 provisioning backends behind adapters is defensible).
  Split only if adapters prove fake.

