## 7. Unified remediation sequence

Ordering principle (both auditors agree): **ownership before archival before rename** — renaming while a token has two owners
multiplies ambiguity; archiving before ownership settles orphans personas.

1. **Publish the machine-readable persona-ownership table** — one row per token, exactly one winner (M§4.5/§9.1; D F2).
   `personas=` exists in `ooda.pkg` for only 3 repos fleet-wide; nothing else is safely decidable without it.
2. **Break the cycles** — `oohash`↔`oob3sum` (→`oohash` per §4.7 + RFC amendment) and `oobuild-fleet`↔`oodeploy` (→`oodeploy`
   per RFC).
3. **Arbitrate multi-host tokens** — `oodns-cloud`/`dns`→`oomesh`; `ooqueue`/`queue`→`oodb-dist`; §4.2/§4.5 owner decisions.
4. **Withdraw the 21 catalog-exposed double-ships** (§6.4) — fixes the *public* surface first.
5. **Archive the ~23 mechanically-ready repos** (§6.1) — after parity proof per repo, not before (RFC 0011 gate).
6. **Fix the spec, not just the code** — RFC 0012 amendments: `oofalse`→`oofalsify`, `oohash` pick, add `ooflash`, record
   `ooconsent`/`ooqueue`/`oonotes`/`oopdf`/`oomail` verdicts; delete phantom `unix_consolidation_blueprint.md` ref; scrub
   `website/llms.txt:35`, `oooffice/README.md:54` (`ooffice`→`oooffice`), 9 `ooagent-*` README lines, `oooda-engine` symlink docs,
   `northstar.oot` L4 list + `status` declaration, 6 `oofzf` AGENTS.md copies, hardcoded host bindings.
7. **Renames after ownership settles** (§6.5): apps → OS → kernel → agents → tools → core.
8. **Native-implementation debt** — `ooflash` shims → native `.oo`; 8 exec-relay persona tables → native impls tested
   **without** upstream binaries present; kill `oodac_cluster.sh`, `mcp_client.oo` fallback, `spawn.oo` aliases after renames
   land.
9. **Extract shared substrate** — apps 16× framework copies + kernel 15-page template + DE 28-file clone-set → `std` imports
   (Rule 1.25 §3); `std`→`std-hw` split; kernel template dedup.
10. **Hygiene & gates** — `link-law` gate in all cloud/agents Makefiles; `.ooda-cache` purge; `8`/`bracket_probe*` debris;
    `bin/`vs`dist/` convention; `install.sh` bare names; `oodac` stale copies; `SRC`-`fsprobe` rebuild defect; `ELF64` README
    lies; extend registry beyond L3 (catalog blindness is why C2 survived); page-gate allowlist for `boundary_257_lines.oo`;
    declare anchor-shim exemptions for the 246/1,857 core violations or schedule cleanup.

---

## 8. Residual risk — what no pass could establish

1. **No builds or tests were run by any of the three passes.** "Ready to archive" = source-structure readiness only; run
   `make all` on each host before deleting any absorbed repo.
2. **mcode's 82-token matrix** is equality-chain extraction; table-driven personas could evade it. Re-derive when building the
   Phase-1 registry.
3. **devin's 104-skeleton count** was sampled, not exhaustively classified (±104).
4. **The tree is live** — `ooflash` landed mid-audit (03:55–03:59 HST). Re-snapshot before executing Phase 5.
5. **`std/anchor.oo` vs `std/hw/anchor.oo`** contradict each other on whether `hw/` is docs-only — the split resolves it
   regardless.
6. **External install scripts** may reference `ooagent-*` applet names outside these trees — verify before scrubbing the 9
   README lines.
7. **`/Projects/idlescreen`** (out of scope) contains desktop-applet literals in ASCII scenes — will trip a naive hostname lint
   if applied repo-wide.

---

## 9. Audit quality assessment

Table columns: | mcode (788 lines) | devin (283 lines)
- **Method** | token-collision matrix, machine-extracted | physical subtree graph + RFC conformance
- **Strength** | complete quantification (82 tokens, 21 catalog), per-line citations, conformance sweep, deepest single defect (
  `std/hw`), only live code bug (port mismatch) | inversions vs RFC, name-semantics layer (cryptic names, ghosts, missing
  coverage), hygiene findings (oofzf copies, debris), skeleton-stub classification
- **Blind spot** | name zoo, skeleton class, debris, `oosqllite` | `std/hw` (biggest scope violation), `oohash`↔`oob3sum` cycle,
  argv0-in-source, hardcoded IPs, catalog-collision enumeration
- **Verified errata** | 3 cosmetic (17→16, 20→21, `ooshell` ghost) | 1 overstatement (`oowm`/`ooterm` "file-for-file")
- **Reliability** | every sampled claim verified | every sampled claim verified

The two passes are genuinely complementary: mcode is the **measurement** pass (counts, matrices, sweeps), devin the
**spec-conformance** pass (RFC adjudication, name semantics, hygiene). Neither alone covers the defect space; together they do.

---

**Bottom line:** RFC 0012's consolidation is directionally right and partially implemented, but ownership was never enforced —
so absorbed names are sold twice, canonical names exist only on paper, and four pairs of binaries point at each other. Publish
the ownership table (step 1) **before** any archive or rename, or every fix re-creates the ambiguity it removes.

*Consensus produced by Devin `wR:p2`, reconciling `naming-audit-devin.md` (283 lines) against `naming-audit-mcode.md` (788
lines) with independent tree verification. Supersedes the earlier `wR:p1` draft of this file. Read-only; no builds/tests
executed.*
